<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">
    <!--
        CVE-2026-66299 (CVSS 7.5) is an uncontrolled resource consumption DoS in the
        WebSocket chat "examples" web application bundled with the Apache Tomcat
        distribution.

        Suppressed because it is not exploitable here, and that reasoning does not depend
        on a version: Spring Boot's embedded Tomcat (spring-boot-starter-tomcat ->
        tomcat-embed-core/-el/-websocket) never deploys the "examples" web application
        that contains the vulnerable chat servlet — only a full Tomcat distribution does.

        Originally added while the project was on tomcat-embed-core 10.1.57, where no
        patched 10.1.x artifact existed on Maven Central. The Spring Boot 4.1 upgrade moved
        the embedded container to the 11.0.x line, so the rule may now match nothing and
        be reported as unused (a warning, not a failure). It is kept rather than deleted
        because the "examples webapp is never deployed" argument holds for every line, so
        it stays correct if this CVE is later scored against 11.0.x too.
    -->
    <suppress>
        <notes>CVE-2026-66299 affects the Tomcat "examples" webapp only, which the embedded Tomcat used by Spring Boot never deploys.</notes>
        <packageUrl regex="true">^pkg:maven/org\.apache\.tomcat\.embed/tomcat\-embed.*@.*$</packageUrl>
        <cve>CVE-2026-66299</cve>
    </suppress>
</suppressions>
